From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:10:22 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] vb-input

The Virtual Boy pad. The device D-pad is the left D-pad and A, B, L, R,
Start and Select are themselves. Beetle VB is plugged as a plain pad
(PLAIN_PAD, the libretro joypad id) so it is answered RETRO_DEVICE_ANALOG
like pcsx, and with vb_right_analog_to_digital enabled it reads the right
analog stick itself as the right D-pad. X and Y never reach the core:
the core reads X as the low battery switch. L2 and R2 stay slot's rewind
and fast forward.

The Right Pad row's ABXY choice is for games that use the right D-pad
as buttons: X, A, B and Y are right up, right, down and left (the
libretro ids L2, R3, L3 and R2 the core maps to them, so ButtonMask gains
L3 and R3), and the console's A and B move to R2 and L2. Then L2 and R2
go to the game the PS1 way, latched at the start of the game, so the
choice applies from the next game, with fast forward on Select+R2 and no
rewind button. A generated cart reads the pad through SCR and SDLR/SDHR
and proves every button and the stick reach the game.
